error[NK2108]: This `return` leaves `w` without `w[i]`.
  --> tests/an_element_of_a_mut_list_left_out_is_refused.nika:9:2
   |
 8 | 	let t = left_out_element_hold(w[i])
   |                                ---- taken out of `w` here
 9 | 	return t.len()
   |  ^^^^^^ leaves the function with the part still out
   |
   = note: `w` is a `mut` parameter, so it is the caller's and is whole whenever the caller can see it. `w[i]` was passed to `left_out_element_hold`, which keeps it, and nothing has put it back.
   = help: Assign `w` (or the part) before the function is left, or build the value by value with `fn f(w: T) -> T`.

